        "author": "IARPA STONESOUP Test and Evaluation team",
        "description": "This test case reads the taint source. If it contains a non-alphanumeric value, the source taint buffer is set to NULL. Subsequently, strcpy is called with the source taint buffer as this source. This causes a null pointer dereference.\nMetadata\n - Base program: PostgreSQL\n - Source Taint: SOCKET\n - Data Type: VOID_POINTER\n - Data Flow: ADDRESS_AS_VARIABLE\n - Control Flow: SET_JUMP_LONG_JUMP",
